# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the op-fusion programme's host-gap package WPH (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the fusion integration branch and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. WPH/ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag the pack's B0 builds from the pushed branch head (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# H10 (INSTRUMENTED, ONE UNPROFILED RUN, WPH-4): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-wph-log = the combined fusion arm (c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all) plus QWEN_FAST_TP4_HOSTGAP_LOG=1 and QWEN_FAST_TP4_HOSTGAP_PROBE=1 and nothing
# else. Not a timing arm (the instrument wraps the host calls and writes about a dozen lines a round): it is the account of WHERE the host gap sits on the arm the owner will run. It writes, per step, [PACKED-HOSTGAP-ROUND]
# (wall and thread CPU, voluntary and involuntary context switches, page faults, every garbage collection, the host calls: copy_host_to_device_tensor 'copy', from_torch 'up', execute_trace 'tnb' non-blocking and 'tb'
# blocking, synchronize_device 'fence', to_torch 'read', each with its count, total and LONGEST single call) and [PACKED-HOSTGAP-SPAN] for the pre-stage of each block, the window, the fence F9, the two quad
# launches, the collect, each verify's stage and readback, and the phases (execute, packed_verify, early_draft, propose_quad, packed_commit); and every 16th eight-live round [PACKED-HOSTGAP-PROBE]: one TIMED synchronize
# right after the two quad launches, so 2Q is measured directly (twoq_ms, from the first non-blocking enqueue). A probe round runs its window after the quads: it is not a round time and the paired timing tool and the reader drop it.
# READ: python3 scripts/ci/hostgap_read.py <container log> --json hostgap.json prints (probe rounds dropped) the rounds, every span's wall and CPU, the SLOW spans (more than 1.5 times their own median; the 22 percent of
# rounds with a quad launch of 5.8-6.4 ms instead of about 2, and writes 2-5 times slower) CLASSIFIED by cause - gc, blocked-copy (one copy or enqueue took the excess while the CPU idled: the command queue was full),
# descheduled (involuntary switches, CPU under 70 percent of wall), cpu-bound, wait - the probe's 2Q, and the share of rounds whose fence wait after the window was under 1 ms (the window is the critical path).
# c2_smoke_check must be clean with the WPH rule (the instrument's engaged line, round and span lines, a probe line once 40 rounds ran). Duration (estimate): 45 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-wph-log
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k
